  "reason": "Evidence: With only two completed experiments, RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% acc while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is very weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether the PCA representation is near-optimal or whether a learned biological encoder (scVI) can substantially improve RNA signal quality. This experiment (config_004: RNA, singleprofile, scvi_n200) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001, changing only the RNA encoder while holding modality and profile setting constant. It directly tests whether a learned, lower-dimensional (200-d) representation can match or exceed a high-dimensional (2000-d) linear one. This is the best next step because the answer determines whether to invest remaining budget in scvi/scgpt-based configurations or to focus on aggregation and fusion strategies with PCA; it reduces uncertainty about a fundamental representation choice that gates many downstream decisions."
}

